host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan fanin -- who wrote an ask is a fact of the region, never of the bytes
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, condense REMEMBER, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. The living REDS rows all carry closure notes -- 80 closed by the count guard, 83 by the ASCII loom, 84 on measurement, 85 reopened and closed with a real check behind it -- so no agent-closable red stood open. Confirmed rather than assumed: tools/living_card_ascii_witness.rish run on metal, GREEN, its planted mojibake control still caught.
think Council rota, lap 456 of the 27-doc d27 -- item 24, active-designing/20260702-184312_the-grain-and-the-crossing.md. Two strands cut this round directly. Values apart, never braided: attribution and fairness are separate properties and stay separate mechanisms, one a comparison against the region, the other a bound per stream. And the seam honesty strand: the host filesystem stands openly as the stand-in for a kernel mapping, named rather than absorbed.
think The last lap's recommend named the crux exactly -- two clients writing one queue, where a single head stops being enough to say who wrote which ask. Reading serial_two_clients.bron showed the declaration already answers half of it: each client owns its own private pair of regions, so each already has its own head, and the server already has a ledger per client. What a second producer really opens is two different questions.
think The first is attribution, and it is the one the arc has been walking toward since carry.rye. Bytes can say anything. A client may write an ask whose text names its sibling as author, and no amount of reading that text catches the lie. The answer is that the server never asks the bytes -- it reads tx_a, and tx_a is a region only client_a may write. The author of an ask is the domain that owns the region it arrived in.
think Made the forgery expressible on purpose. An ask that carried no author would attribute correctly and prove nothing; ask_text names its author precisely so a claim can be checked against the region, and a disagreement answers Misattributed. Chose refusal over silent correction -- the server knows the true author and could overrule the claim, yet an ask that lies about itself is a fact an operator wants to see rather than one the server quietly repairs.
think The second is fairness, which arrives without a single wrong byte. A server that empties one client's queue before looking at the next lets a busy producer delay a quiet one for as long as it keeps writing. A declared per-pass take answers it: one sweep draws at most per_pass from each stream, so a client on a full queue and a client with one ask are both served on the same pass.
think The plan wire needed a shape for many streams. Kept queue.rye's five colon-separated fields and made three of them comma-joined lists of equal length -- heard, mine, peer, one entry per stream -- so a single-client verb rides the same wire with lists of one. Unequal lengths are refused rather than paired with whatever sits at the index, and a list longer than the server holds is refused rather than truncated.
obs The pairing of region to peer belongs to the supervisor, which reads the declaration; letting the server derive it from name conventions would have made a naming habit load-bearing. The plan word carries it, so the document remains the source.
obs The first wall answered NotGranted rather than the WriteDenied I expected. That is the truer refusal and it was written down as such: client_b holds no grant at all on tx_a, so the wall stands one step earlier than it does for a read-only holder. Measurement corrected the prose rather than the prose bending the expectation.
obs The Unheard wall had to run before the impostor step, since a misattributed ask left standing meets every later sweep first. Ordering the wall plan by what each step leaves behind is the same discipline the batch plan already keeps.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass after the two ordering corrections; both RED probes proven before the green was trusted, per the arc's habit.
loom witness=caravan_fanin_witness asks=7 producers=2 rings=3 sweeps=2 streams=4 per_pass=2 busy_take=2 quiet_take=1
loom red_probe=trust_the_bytes result=impostor_ask_served_as_genuine outcome=carried
loom red_probe=shared_budget result=quiet_client_served_zero outcome=bytes_differed
file caravan/fanin.rye the ring itself -- attribution by region, a sweep bounded per stream, five verbs each in its own process
file tools/caravan_fanin_witness.rish the witness -- GREEN on metal, every claim read natively with contains
file caravan/README.md the ladder gains its seventeenth row and the prose that says why the region names the author
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to fanin; the queue edge condenses into the prior-edges line
recommend keep-going -- next the silent-consumer shape: a stream whose peer never drains, where a server holding a full queue for a client that has stopped reading must choose between blocking every other stream, dropping by declared policy, or refusing the wire. No key, no funds, no gate.
